Third-party software
====================

No third-party code is bundled yet.

hakutaku is pre-release, and its repository holds no code so far. The analysis engines are not
bundled: `hakutaku engines install` will install them separately, at versions pinned with integrity
hashes in engines.lock.json. Each project is credited here when it is added, with the copyright line
copied from its licence file at the pinned version. The full licence texts of anything the package
bundles will be in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/.


Analysis engines: planned, not bundled
--------------------------------------

scip-typescript (Sourcegraph)
  https://github.com/sourcegraph/scip-typescript
  Licence: Apache-2.0
  Planned use: an engine, run as a separate program. TypeScript call sites and references, bound by
  the compiler.

dependency-cruiser
  https://github.com/sverweij/dependency-cruiser
  Licence: MIT
  Planned use: an engine, run as a separate program. TypeScript and JavaScript import edges, cycles
  and layer rules.

grimp
  https://github.com/python-grimp/grimp
  Licence: BSD-2-Clause
  Planned use: an engine, a Python library that hakutaku's driver runs. The Python import graph.

ast-grep, with tree-sitter inside
  https://github.com/ast-grep/ast-grep
  https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter
  Licence: MIT (both)
  Planned use: an engine, its command-line program run as a separate program. The outline that mints
  every definition's ID, call sites, string literals and the shell rules.

scip-python (Sourcegraph), built on Pyright (Microsoft)
  https://github.com/sourcegraph/scip-python
  https://github.com/microsoft/pyright
  Licence: MIT (both)
  Planned use: an optional engine, run as a separate program at deep detail only. Python call sites,
  bound by the compiler.

TypeScript (Microsoft)
  https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript
  Licence: Apache-2.0
  Planned use: none directly. It runs inside scip-typescript and dependency-cruiser.

SCIP, the index format (Sourcegraph)
  https://github.com/scip-code/scip
  Licence: Apache-2.0
  Planned use: hakutaku will decode the SCIP indexes that the engines write.
